 'The copied planner is wrapped with the full compiled carriage ranges, removing the old proposal-only R-carriage cap. RRT-Connect has at least 65 seconds, 12-second restarts, staging proposals and 16 shortcut trials; 20 mm search edges remain proposals only. Accepted routes receive model-derived ≤4 mm point-displacement replay, endpoint 5 mm/3° checks, all check-wrench combinations, rated-envelope demand and grip checks. Working strokes must also follow their required Cartesian geometry; an RRT detour cannot replace washing or peeling. Cartesian continuation now includes carriage redundancy and equivalent-angle rebasing.', '',
 f"The retained discrete ledger has {len(seq['expanded_strokes'])} expanded strokes, {len(seq['expanded_connections'])} connections, {len(seq['events'])} events and {seq['unverified_required_events']} required event paths; {len(seq['removed_idempotent_commands'])} idempotent commands are removed. Four complete raw inputs total 0.57 kg, with single-valued ownership and {len(seq['discrete_state_chain_errors'])} discrete chain errors. Full food remains until an accepted partition exists; unsupported cuts cannot delete or shrink bodies. Obsolete R211 lid/pusher proxies are removed from the new persistent scene, while the full BFP exterior stays. Exact new interfaces are marked missing, never credited as a replacement model.", '',
